<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="God">
  <data key="d0">God</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">God is portrayed as the divine Creator of heaven, earth, light, plants, animals, and humanity. God creates man and woman in the divine likeness, blesses them, gives commands, and rests after completing creation. God establishes human accountability for bloodshed and is associated with the angels seen in Jacob’s ladder vision.

God walks with Enoch and takes him, observes human wickedness, and instructs Noah to build an ark for the destruction of corrupt flesh. Identified also as the LORD, God brings the Flood, remembers Noah, sends a wind over the earth, speaks to and blesses Noah and his sons, establishes a covenant, and promises never again to destroy all living things by such a catastrophe. God hears Hagar’s affliction, appears and speaks to Abraham, protects Sarah, enables Isaac’s birth, heals Abimelech’s household, and establishes covenants and promises concerning Abraham’s descendants. God instructs Abraham regarding the offering, is feared and obeyed by him, promises Isaac, blesses Ishmael, investigates the wrongdoing of Sodom and Gomorrah, and destroys the cities of the plain while rescuing Lot for Abraham’s sake.

God blesses Isaac with heavenly dew, earthly abundance, grain, and wine. As the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, God hears prayers, observes affliction, enables conception, opens Rachel’s womb, and graciously gives Jacob children. God protects Jacob from Laban, blesses Laban for Jacob’s sake, alters the cattle’s breeding, appears to Laban in a dream, and serves as witness and judge. God directs Jacob to Bethel to dwell and build an altar, accompanies him with divine terror, answers him in distress, promises land and descendants, and commands his return to his ancestral land and kindred.

God is identified by Joseph as the authority against whom sexual wrongdoing is sin and as the source of dream interpretation. God reveals future events, provides Pharaoh’s answer through Joseph, establishes the prophesied outcomes, and raises Joseph to authority in Egypt to preserve life. Joseph fears and credits God for his circumstances, including forgetfulness and fruitfulness, while his brothers invoke God in recognizing revealed iniquity and questioning their returned money. God appears to Jacob in a nighttime vision as the God of Isaac, promises to accompany him into Egypt, gives Joseph his sons, feeds Jacob throughout his life, blesses his descendants, and remains with his family. Ultimately, God turns intended evil toward good, saves many people, visits Israel’s children, and fulfills the oath made to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790124751</data>
