</node>
<node id="Heaven">
  <data key="d0">Heaven</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Heaven is the created celestial domain identified with the firmament and the upper realm. In the flood narrative, its windows open to release rain, making Heaven the heavenly region associated with the onset of the Deluge.

Heaven is described as belonging to the Most High God and as the setting from which Abram observes the stars. It is also the source from which the LORD sends brimstone and fire upon Sodom and Gomorrah, and from which dew descends in the blessing given to Isaac.

In Jacob’s dream, Heaven is the upper destination reached by the ladder and is associated with the gate revealed in his sacred vision. This connection leads Jacob to name the place Bethel, presenting Heaven both as a divine realm and as the celestial destination linked to the gateway between Heaven and earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790124750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Earth">
  <data key="d0">Earth</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Earth is the created terrestrial domain and inhabited world containing dry land, the ground, vegetation, animals, and humanity. It is presented as the realm possessed by the Most High God and as the source of agricultural abundance in Isaac’s blessing.

Earth is also the setting of major human events and divine judgment. Cain was cursed and driven away from it, and it became corrupt and filled with violence because of human wickedness. The terrestrial world was subsequently covered by the waters of the flood; the waters later receded, the earth dried, and it was designated as the place where living creatures would multiply.

After the flood, Earth was replenished and overspread by Noah’s descendants and included within God’s covenant. It is also the world across whose surface the LORD scattered people, emphasizing its role as the inhabited realm of human communities and history.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790124750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Darkness">
  <data key="d0">Darkness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Darkness covers the deep and is separated from light by God.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790124745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deep">
  <data key="d0">Deep</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The deep is the primordial watery expanse over which darkness lies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790124745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spirit Of God">
  <data key="d0">Spirit Of God</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Spirit of God moves upon the face of the waters during creation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790124745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Waters">
  <data key="d0">Waters</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The waters cover the primordial earth and are divided by the firmament.&lt;SEP&gt;The waters prevailed over the earth, covered the mountains, gradually abated, and eventually dried from the earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790124745</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Genesis">
  <data key="d0">Genesis</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Genesis is a biblical book containing an account of creation, including the formation of heaven, earth, living creatures, and humanity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Light">
  <data key="d0">Light</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Light is created by God, separated from darkness, and associated with the day.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Day">
  <data key="d0">Day</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Day is the name God gives to the light and is distinguished from night.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Night">
  <data key="d0">Night</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Night is the name God gives to the darkness and is distinguished from day.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Firmament">
  <data key="d0">Firmament</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The firmament is an expanse made by God to divide the waters and later called Heaven.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seas">
  <data key="d0">Seas</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Seas are the gathered waters separated from the dry land.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grass">
  <data key="d0">Grass</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Grass is vegetation brought forth by the earth as seed-bearing plant life.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Herb">
  <data key="d0">Herb</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Herbs are seed-bearing plants provided as food for humanity and living creatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fruit Tree">
  <data key="d0">Fruit Tree</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Fruit trees are plants that produce fruit containing seed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stars">
  <data key="d0">Stars</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Stars are celestial lights made by God and placed in the firmament.&lt;SEP&gt;The stars are celestial objects used by the LORD to illustrate the innumerable future seed of Abram.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Living Creatures">
  <data key="d0">Living Creatures</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Living creatures include aquatic animals, birds, cattle, creeping things, and beasts of the earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Great Whales">
  <data key="d0">Great Whales</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Great whales are large aquatic creatures created by God.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fowl">
  <data key="d0">Fowl</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Fowl are winged creatures created to fly above the earth and multiply.&lt;SEP&gt;Fowl were among the living creatures destroyed by the waters and were later brought out of the ark and included in Noah's offerings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beast Of The Earth">
  <data key="d0">Beast Of The Earth</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Beasts of the earth are land animals created according to their kinds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Creeping Thing">
  <data key="d0">Creeping Thing</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Creeping things are terrestrial creatures that move upon the earth.&lt;SEP&gt;Creeping things were among the living creatures that the LORD said would be destroyed from the face of the earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Man">
  <data key="d0">Man</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Man represents male and female humanity created in the image and likeness of God.&lt;SEP&gt;Man refers to humanity, which multiplied on the earth, became wicked, and was subject to divine judgment.&lt;SEP&gt;Humanity, whose blood is subject to divine accountability and whose creation is described as being in God's image.&lt;SEP&gt;Man was among the living beings who died during the flood and was referenced in God's promise concerning the ground.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fish">
  <data key="d0">Fish</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Fish are aquatic creatures placed under human dominion.&lt;SEP&gt;Fish of the sea were described as being delivered into the hand of Noah and his sons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Evening">
  <data key="d0">Evening</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Evening is the period paired with morning to mark the successive days of creation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Morning">
  <data key="d0">Morning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Morning is the period paired with evening to mark the successive days of creation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="First Day">
  <data key="d0">First Day</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The first day is the creation period during which God creates light and separates it from darkness.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Second Day">
  <data key="d0">Second Day</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The second day is the creation period during which God creates and names the firmament.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Third Day">
  <data key="d0">Third Day</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The third day is the creation period during which God gathers the waters, reveals dry land, and brings forth vegetation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fourth Day">
  <data key="d0">Fourth Day</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The fourth day is the creation period during which God makes lights for the firmament to govern day and night.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fifth Day">
  <data key="d0">Fifth Day</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The fifth day is the creation period during which God creates aquatic creatures and winged fowl.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Signs">
  <data key="d0">Signs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Signs are purposes assigned to the lights in the firmament.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seasons">
  <data key="d0">Seasons</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Seasons are periods that the lights in the firmament are assigned to mark.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Years">
  <data key="d0">Years</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Years are time periods that the lights in the firmament are assigned to mark.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Greater Light">
  <data key="d0">Greater Light</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The greater light is a celestial light made to rule the day.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lesser Light">
  <data key="d0">Lesser Light</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The lesser light is a celestial light made to rule the night.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fruit">
  <data key="d0">Fruit</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">The fruit came from the trees of the garden, including the tree in the midst of the garden, and was eaten by Eve and Adam.&lt;SEP&gt;Fruit is produced by fruit trees and contains seed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adam">
  <data key="d0">Adam</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adam is the man formed by God from the dust of the ground, placed in the Garden of Eden, and given authority to name living creatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Adam is Eve's husband who ate the forbidden fruit, hid in the garden, received judgment from the LORD God, and became the father of Cain and Abel.&lt;SEP&gt;Adam is the first human described in the generations, created in God's likeness, and the father of Seth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Woman">
  <data key="d0">Woman</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Woman is formed from Adam’s rib and brought to Adam as a companion and wife.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serpent">
  <data key="d0">Serpent</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">The Serpent is described as more subtle than the beasts of the field and questions the Woman about God’s command.&lt;SEP&gt;The serpent beguiled Eve, denied that eating the forbidden fruit would cause death, and was cursed by the LORD God.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Garden of Eden">
  <data key="d0">Garden of Eden</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Garden of Eden is a garden planted by God eastward in Eden, containing trees, including the Tree of Life and the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil.&lt;SEP&gt;The Garden of Eden is the garden where the tree in the midst of the garden and the tree of life stood, where Adam and Eve hid, and from which Adam was sent away.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eden">
  <data key="d0">Eden</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Eden is the region where God plants the garden and from which a river flows to water the garden.&lt;SEP&gt;Eden is the location used to orient the land of Nod, which lies east of Eden.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tree of Life">
  <data key="d0">Tree of Life</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The Tree of Life stands in the midst of the Garden of Eden.&lt;SEP&gt;The tree of life was a tree whose fruit could enable continued life, and the way to it was guarded after Adam's expulsion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil">
  <data key="d0">Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil stands in the Garden of Eden, and God forbids Adam to eat its fruit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pison">
  <data key="d0">Pison</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pison is the first river flowing from Eden and encircles the land of Havilah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Havilah">
  <data key="d0">Havilah</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Havilah is the land encircled by the river Pison and is described as containing gold, bdellium, and onyx stone.&lt;SEP&gt;A son of Cush.&lt;SEP&gt;Havilah is identified as a son of Cush and as a son of Joktan.&lt;SEP&gt;Havilah is the western limit of the region where Ishmael's descendants dwelt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gihon">
  <data key="d0">Gihon</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gihon is the second river flowing from Eden and encircles the land of Ethiopia.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ethiopia">
  <data key="d0">Ethiopia</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Ethiopia is the land encircled by the river Gihon.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hiddekel">
  <data key="d0">Hiddekel</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hiddekel is the third river flowing from Eden and runs toward the east of Assyria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Assyria">
  <data key="d0">Assyria</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Assyria is the region toward which the river Hiddekel runs eastward.&lt;SEP&gt;Assyria is the direction toward which the region of Ishmael's descendants extended from Shur.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Euphrates">
  <data key="d0">Euphrates</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Euphrates is the fourth river associated with the river flowing from Eden.&lt;SEP&gt;The Euphrates is the great river marking the eastern boundary of the land promised by the LORD to Abram’s seed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heavens">
  <data key="d0">Heavens</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The heavens are part of the created heavens and earth finished by God.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gold">
  <data key="d0">Gold</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gold is a valuable substance found in the land of Havilah and described as good.&lt;SEP&gt;A form of wealth in which Abram is described as being very rich.&lt;SEP&gt;A valuable material included among Abraham's possessions and used for Rebekah's earring and bracelets.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bdellium">
  <data key="d0">Bdellium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Bdellium is a substance found in the land of Havilah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Onyx Stone">
  <data key="d0">Onyx Stone</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Onyx stone is a stone found in the land of Havilah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sixth Day">
  <data key="d0">Sixth Day</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The sixth day marks the completion of the creation described before the heavens and earth are finished.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seventh Day">
  <data key="d0">Seventh Day</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The seventh day is the day on which God ends the work of creation, rests, blesses the day, and sanctifies it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beasts of the Earth">
  <data key="d0">Beasts of the Earth</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Beasts of the earth are living creatures created by God and given green herbs for food.&lt;SEP&gt;Land animals placed under human authority and included among the living creatures covered by God's covenant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fowl of the Air">
  <data key="d0">Fowl of the Air</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Fowl of the air are living creatures created by God and given green herbs for food.&lt;SEP&gt;Birds placed under human authority and included among the living creatures covered by God's covenant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Green Herb">
  <data key="d0">Green Herb</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Green herbs are given by God as food for beasts, fowl, and other living creatures.&lt;SEP&gt;The green herb was identified as food comparable to the provision of every living moving thing.&lt;SEP&gt;Vegetation given to humanity as food.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plants of the Field">
  <data key="d0">Plants of the Field</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Plants of the field are described before they grow in the earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ground">
  <data key="d0">Ground</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The ground was cursed because of Adam, produced thorns and thistles, and was the source to which Adam would return.&lt;SEP&gt;The ground is watered by mist and provides the dust from which God forms Adam.&lt;SEP&gt;The ground receives Abel's blood and no longer yields its strength to Cain.&lt;SEP&gt;The ground was covered by waters, later became dry, and was mentioned in relation to God's promise not to curse it again.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dust">
  <data key="d0">Dust</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Dust from the ground is the material from which God forms Adam.&lt;SEP&gt;Dust was the material from which Adam was taken and to which Adam would return, and it was also assigned as the serpent's food.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breath of Life">
  <data key="d0">Breath of Life</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The breath of life is breathed by God into Adam’s nostrils, causing Adam to become a living soul.&lt;SEP&gt;The life-giving breath present in living creatures and used to describe those destroyed outside the ark.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Living Soul">
  <data key="d0">Living Soul</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">A living soul describes Adam after God breathes the breath of life into Adam.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rib">
  <data key="d0">Rib</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A rib taken from Adam is used by God to form the Woman.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="River">
  <data key="d0">River</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A river flows from Eden to water the garden and divides into four heads.&lt;SEP&gt;The river beside which Pharaoh stood in his dream, from which the cattle emerged.&lt;SEP&gt;The river is the setting beside which Pharaoh sees the cattle in his dream.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eve">
  <data key="d0">Eve</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Eve is Adam's wife and the woman who ate fruit from the tree in the midst of the garden, gave fruit to Adam, and was identified as the mother of all living.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LORD God">
  <data key="d0">LORD God</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The LORD God commanded Adam and Eve not to eat from the tree in the midst of the garden, questioned them after the eating, judged the serpent, Eve, and Adam, clothed Adam and Eve, and sent Adam out of Eden.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tree in the Midst of the Garden">
  <data key="d0">Tree in the Midst of the Garden</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The tree in the midst of the garden was the tree from which the LORD God prohibited Adam and Eve from eating.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fig Leaves">
  <data key="d0">Fig Leaves</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig leaves were sewn together by Adam and Eve to make coverings after their eyes were opened.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aprons">
  <data key="d0">Aprons</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Aprons were coverings made by Adam and Eve from sewn fig leaves.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Coats of Skins">
  <data key="d0">Coats of Skins</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Coats of skins were made by the LORD God and given to Adam and Eve as clothing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cherubims">
  <data key="d0">Cherubims</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Cherubims were placed at the east of the Garden of Eden to keep the way to the tree of life.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flaming Sword">
  <data key="d0">Flaming Sword</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The flaming sword turned in every direction and was placed to keep the way to the tree of life.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cain">
  <data key="d0">Cain</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cain was Adam and Eve's son, a tiller of the ground who brought an offering from the ground and became angry when the LORD God rejected the offering.&lt;SEP&gt;Cain is Adam's son who presents an offering, kills Abel, receives a curse and protective mark from the LORD, leaves the LORD's presence, dwells in Nod, and fathers Enoch.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abel">
  <data key="d0">Abel</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Abel was Adam and Eve's son and a keeper of sheep who brought the firstlings and fat of his flock as an offering to the LORD God.&lt;SEP&gt;Abel is Cain's brother whom Cain kills in the field.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sheep">
  <data key="d0">Sheep</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Sheep were tended by Abel, who kept a flock and brought its firstlings and fat as an offering.&lt;SEP&gt;Livestock given to Abram as part of Pharaoh's favorable treatment of him because of Sarai.&lt;SEP&gt;Sheep belonged to the flocks gathered at the well and were watered and tended by Rachel and Jacob.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Offering">
  <data key="d0">Offering</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An offering was brought to the LORD God by Cain from the fruit of the ground and by Abel from the firstlings and fat of his flock.&lt;SEP&gt;The offering is presented by Cain but receives no respect from the LORD.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sin">
  <data key="d0">Sin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sin is described as lying at the door when a person does not do well.&lt;SEP&gt;Sin is described as lying at the door and connected with whether Cain does well.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trees of the Garden">
  <data key="d0">Trees of the Garden</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The trees of the garden produced fruit that the woman said Adam and Eve could eat.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beasts of the Field">
  <data key="d0">Beasts of the Field</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Beasts of the field were included among the animals above which the serpent was cursed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seed">
  <data key="d0">Seed</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Seed represents the descendants of the serpent and the woman in the stated enmity between them.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram's descendants, whom the LORD promises will inherit the land and become as numerous as the dust of the earth.&lt;SEP&gt;The descendants of Abram to whom the LORD promised the land of Canaan.&lt;SEP&gt;The descendants promised to Abram, who were to become as numerous as the dust of the earth and continue forever.&lt;SEP&gt;Seed was provided by Joseph so the people could sow the land after selling their fields to Pharaoh.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thorns and Thistles">
  <data key="d0">Thorns and Thistles</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Thorns and thistles were said to grow from the cursed ground for Adam.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Herb of the Field">
  <data key="d0">Herb of the Field</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The herb of the field was food that Adam would eat after the ground was cursed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bread">
  <data key="d0">Bread</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Bread was food that Adam would eat through the sweat of his face.&lt;SEP&gt;Food that Abraham gives to Hagar when sending Hagar and Hagar's son away.&lt;SEP&gt;Bread is food prepared by Rebekah and given to Jacob to present to Isaac.&lt;SEP&gt;Bread was identified by Jacob as food that God might provide during Jacob's journey.&lt;SEP&gt;The food requested by the Egyptians and available in Egypt during the famine.&lt;SEP&gt;Bread is the food Joseph distributed to households and exchanged for money, horses, flocks, cattle, and asses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children">
  <data key="d0">Children</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Children were to be brought forth by the woman in sorrow.&lt;SEP&gt;Laban's children were claimed by Laban during the dispute and were included in the covenant context.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Good and Evil">
  <data key="d0">Good and Evil</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Good and evil are forms of knowledge associated with the opened eyes of Adam and Eve and the condition of becoming like gods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gods">
  <data key="d0">Gods</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Gods are beings whom the serpent claimed Adam and Eve would resemble after eating the fruit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sorrow">
  <data key="d0">Sorrow</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sorrow was assigned to the woman in conception and childbirth and to Adam in labor for food.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Punishment">
  <data key="d0">Punishment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cain describes Cain's punishment as greater than Cain can bear.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vengeance">
  <data key="d0">Vengeance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vengeance is prescribed sevenfold against anyone who kills Cain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mark Upon Cain">
  <data key="d0">Mark Upon Cain</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The mark is placed upon Cain by the LORD to prevent anyone who finds Cain from killing Cain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Land of Nod">
  <data key="d0">Land of Nod</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The land of Nod is the eastern land where Cain dwells after leaving the LORD's presence.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cain's Wife">
  <data key="d0">Cain's Wife</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cain's unnamed wife conceives and bears Enoch.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enoch">
  <data key="d0">Enoch</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Enoch is Cain's son, the namesake of a city, and the father of Irad.&lt;SEP&gt;Enoch lived sixty-five years before begetting Methuselah, walked with God, and was taken by God at three hundred and sixty-five years.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="City of Enoch">
  <data key="d0">City of Enoch</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The city is built by Cain and named after Cain's son Enoch.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Irad">
  <data key="d0">Irad</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Irad is Enoch's son and the father of Mehujael.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mehujael">
  <data key="d0">Mehujael</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Mehujael is Irad's son and the father of Methusael.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methusael">
  <data key="d0">Methusael</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Methusael is Mehujael's son and the father of Lamech.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lamech">
  <data key="d0">Lamech</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lamech has two wives, Adah and Zillah, fathers several children, and claims to have slain a man and a young man.&lt;SEP&gt;Lamech lived one hundred and eighty-two years before begetting Noah, named Noah, lived five hundred and ninety-five additional years, and died at seven hundred and seventy-seven years.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adah">
  <data key="d0">Adah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adah is Lamech's wife and the mother of Jabal and Jubal.&lt;SEP&gt;A daughter of Elon the Hittite and a wife of Esau who bore Eliphaz.&lt;SEP&gt;Adah is Esau's wife and the mother of Eliphaz.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-037</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zillah">
  <data key="d0">Zillah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zillah is Lamech's wife and the mother of Tubalcain and Naamah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jabal">
  <data key="d0">Jabal</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Jabal is Adah's son and is described as the father of people who dwell in tents and keep cattle.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jubal">
  <data key="d0">Jubal</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Jubal is Adah's son and is described as the father of musicians who handle the harp and organ.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tubalcain">
  <data key="d0">Tubalcain</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Tubalcain is Zillah's son and an instructor of every artificer in brass and iron.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Naamah">
  <data key="d0">Naamah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Naamah is Zillah's daughter and Tubalcain's sister.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adam's Wife">
  <data key="d0">Adam's Wife</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Adam's unnamed wife bears Seth again and identifies Seth as another seed appointed in place of Abel.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seth">
  <data key="d0">Seth</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Seth is Adam's son, appointed as another seed in place of Abel, and the father of Enos.&lt;SEP&gt;Seth lived nine hundred and twelve years before dying.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enos">
  <data key="d0">Enos</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Enos is Seth's son and the father of Cainan.&lt;SEP&gt;Enos lived ninety years before begetting Cainan, lived eight hundred and fifteen additional years, and died at nine hundred and five years.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cainan">
  <data key="d0">Cainan</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cainan is Enos's son, born after Enos lives seventy years.&lt;SEP&gt;Cainan lived seventy years before begetting Mahalaleel, lived eight hundred and forty additional years, and died at nine hundred and ten years.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Field">
  <data key="d0">Field</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The field is the place where Cain rises against Abel and kills Abel.&lt;SEP&gt;An outdoor area to which Esau went to hunt venison.&lt;SEP&gt;The field is the parcel of land where Jacob spreads his tent and which Jacob purchases from the children of Hamor.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-034</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tents">
  <data key="d0">Tents</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tents are dwellings associated with the people for whom Jabal is described as the father.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Harp">
  <data key="d0">Harp</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The harp is a musical instrument associated with the people for whom Jubal is described as the father.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Organ">
  <data key="d0">Organ</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The organ is a musical instrument associated with the people for whom Jubal is described as the father.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brass">
  <data key="d0">Brass</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Brass is a material used by artificers whom Tubalcain instructs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iron">
  <data key="d0">Iron</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron is a material used by artificers whom Tubalcain instructs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mahalaleel">
  <data key="d0">Mahalaleel</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Mahalaleel lived sixty-five years before begetting Jared, lived eight hundred and thirty additional years, and died at eight hundred and ninety-five years.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jared">
  <data key="d0">Jared</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Jared lived one hundred and sixty-two years before begetting Enoch, lived eight hundred additional years, and died at nine hundred and sixty-two years.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methuselah">
  <data key="d0">Methuselah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Methuselah lived one hundred and eighty-seven years before begetting Lamech, lived seven hundred and eighty-two additional years, and died at nine hundred and sixty-nine years.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noah">
  <data key="d0">Noah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Noah was described as just and perfect in his generations, walked with God, found grace with the LORD, and begat Shem, Ham, and Japheth.&lt;SEP&gt;A righteous man commanded by God to build the ark, gather provisions and living creatures, and enter the ark with his household.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah remained alive in the ark, released a raven and a dove, removed the ark covering, left the ark with his family, and built an altar to God.&lt;SEP&gt;A man who receives God's covenant, fathers Shem, Ham, and Japheth, plants a vineyard, drinks wine, and lives after the flood for three hundred and fifty years.&lt;SEP&gt;Noah is identified as the ancestor of the families and nations described after the flood.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shem">
  <data key="d0">Shem</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Shem was one of the three sons begotten by Noah.&lt;SEP&gt;A son of Noah who enters the ark with Noah, Noah's wife, and the wives of Noah's sons.&lt;SEP&gt;A son of Noah who helps cover Noah's nakedness and whose tents receive Japheth.&lt;SEP&gt;Shem is identified as a son of Noah, the father of Eber, and the ancestor of Elam, Asshur, Arphaxad, Lud, and Aram.&lt;SEP&gt;A patriarch who begat Arphaxad and later had additional sons and daughters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ham">
  <data key="d0">Ham</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ham was one of the three sons begotten by Noah.&lt;SEP&gt;A son of Noah who enters the ark with Noah, Noah's wife, and the wives of Noah's sons.&lt;SEP&gt;A son of Noah, the father of Canaan, who sees Noah's nakedness and tells his brothers.&lt;SEP&gt;Ham is identified as the father of Cush, Mizraim, Phut, and Canaan, and as an ancestor of nations and families.&lt;SEP&gt;A place where Chedorlaomer's forces defeated the Zuzims.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Japheth">
  <data key="d0">Japheth</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Japheth was one of the three sons begotten by Noah.&lt;SEP&gt;A son of Noah who enters the ark with Noah, Noah's wife, and the wives of Noah's sons.&lt;SEP&gt;A son of Noah who helps cover Noah's nakedness and is described as dwelling in Shem's tents.&lt;SEP&gt;Japheth is identified as the elder brother of Shem.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sons Of God">
  <data key="d0">Sons Of God</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The sons of God saw the daughters of men, took chosen women as wives, and fathered children who became mighty men of renown.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Daughters Of Men">
  <data key="d0">Daughters Of Men</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The daughters of men were regarded as fair and were taken as wives by the sons of God.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Giants">
  <data key="d0">Giants</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Giants were present on the earth during the stated period and afterward.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ark">
  <data key="d0">Ark</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The ark was an instructed vessel to be made from gopher wood, divided into rooms, and covered inside and outside with pitch; its stated dimensions were three hundred cubits long, fifty cubits wide, and thirty cubits high.&lt;SEP&gt;A large vessel commanded by God and built by Noah from gopher wood, with rooms, a window, a side door, and three stories.&lt;SEP&gt;The ark carried Noah, his family, and living creatures; the ark rested on the mountains of Ararat and was later opened and left.&lt;SEP&gt;The vessel from which Noah's sons and living creatures go forth after the flood.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beast">
  <data key="d0">Beast</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Beasts were among the living creatures that the LORD said would be destroyed from the face of the earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fowls Of The Air">
  <data key="d0">Fowls Of The Air</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Fowls of the air were among the living creatures that the LORD said would be destroyed from the face of the earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flesh">
  <data key="d0">Flesh</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Flesh describes living beings whose ways had become corrupt upon the earth and whom God said would be destroyed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gopher Wood">
  <data key="d0">Gopher Wood</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The wood specified by God as the construction material for the ark.&lt;SEP&gt;Gopher wood was the material from which God instructed Noah to make the ark.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pitch">
  <data key="d0">Pitch</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A substance used to coat the inside and outside of the ark.&lt;SEP&gt;Pitch was the substance used to cover the ark inside and outside.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noah's Wife">
  <data key="d0">Noah's Wife</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The wife of Noah who enters the ark with Noah and Noah's sons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wives of Noah's Sons">
  <data key="d0">Wives of Noah's Sons</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The three wives of Noah's sons who enter the ark with Noah's household.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flood">
  <data key="d0">Flood</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A catastrophic inundation brought by God that covers the earth, lifts the ark, and causes living creatures outside the ark to die.&lt;SEP&gt;A destructive flood whose waters are stated not to destroy all flesh again under the covenant.&lt;SEP&gt;The flood occurring before Shem begat Arphaxad.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rain">
  <data key="d0">Rain</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Rain caused by God to fall upon the earth for forty days and forty nights.&lt;SEP&gt;The rain from heaven was restrained as the floodwaters began to abate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Great Deep">
  <data key="d0">Great Deep</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The great deep whose fountains break up during the onset of the flood.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Food">
  <data key="d0">Food</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Edible provisions gathered by Noah for himself and the living creatures in the ark.&lt;SEP&gt;Food is the commodity that Israel's sons travel to Egypt to purchase.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-046</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clean Beasts">
  <data key="d0">Clean Beasts</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Animals classified as clean, taken into the ark by sevens, consisting of male and female pairs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unclean Beasts">
  <data key="d0">Unclean Beasts</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Animals classified as not clean, taken into the ark by pairs consisting of a male and a female.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fowls">
  <data key="d0">Fowls</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Birds taken into the ark by sevens or pairs, with male and female representatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Creeping Things">
  <data key="d0">Creeping Things</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Creeping animals of the earth taken into the ark as representatives of their kinds.&lt;SEP&gt;Creeping things were among the living creatures destroyed by the waters and were later brought out of the ark.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mountains">
  <data key="d0">Mountains</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Elevated landforms covered by the rising floodwaters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ark Dimensions">
  <data key="d0">Ark Dimensions</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The specified dimensions of the ark: three hundred cubits in length, fifty cubits in breadth, and thirty cubits in height.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ark Rooms">
  <data key="d0">Ark Rooms</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Compartments commanded for construction inside the ark.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ark Window">
  <data key="d0">Ark Window</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An opening constructed in the ark and finished above.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ark Door">
  <data key="d0">Ark Door</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An entrance set in the side of the ark.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ark Stories">
  <data key="d0">Ark Stories</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The lower, second, and third levels specified for the ark.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Living Things">
  <data key="d0">Living Things</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Living creatures brought into the ark in male and female pairs or according to their kinds.&lt;SEP&gt;Living things, including humans and animals, were destroyed by the flood and later brought out of the ark to multiply.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fountains of the Great Deep">
  <data key="d0">Fountains of the Great Deep</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sources of water that break open at the beginning of the flood.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Hills">
  <data key="d0">High Hills</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Elevated landforms covered by the floodwaters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dry Land">
  <data key="d0">Dry Land</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Terrestrial ground on which living creatures exist and from which the flood destroys them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seven Days">
  <data key="d0">Seven Days</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A seven-day period preceding the arrival of the floodwaters and the onset of rainfall.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Forty Days and Forty Nights">
  <data key="d0">Forty Days and Forty Nights</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The stated duration of rainfall and the period during which the flood remains upon the earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noah's Age">
  <data key="d0">Noah's Age</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Noah's stated age of six hundred years when the floodwaters come upon the earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mountains Of Ararat">
  <data key="d0">Mountains Of Ararat</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The mountains of Ararat were the location where the ark rested after the waters began to recede.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raven">
  <data key="d0">Raven</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">The raven was released by Noah and flew back and forth until the waters dried from the earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dove">
  <data key="d0">Dove</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">The dove was released by Noah several times to determine whether the waters had abated; the dove eventually did not return.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Olive Leaf">
  <data key="d0">Olive Leaf</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The olive leaf was carried in the dove's mouth and indicated to Noah that the waters had abated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Altar">
  <data key="d0">Altar</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The altar was built by Noah for burnt offerings to God using clean beasts and clean fowl.&lt;SEP&gt;A structure built by Abram at locations where he worships and calls upon the name of the LORD.&lt;SEP&gt;A worship structure built by Abram in the plain of Mamre unto the LORD.&lt;SEP&gt;Altar built by Abraham at the place designated by God for the burnt offering.&lt;SEP&gt;A structure Isaac built at Beersheba for calling upon the name of the LORD.&lt;SEP&gt;An altar is the structure Jacob is commanded to build at Bethel for God.&lt;SEP&gt;A structure Jacob built at Bethel for God.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beasts">
  <data key="d0">Beasts</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Beasts were among the living creatures destroyed by the waters and were later brought out of the ark.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noah's Sons">
  <data key="d0">Noah's Sons</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Noah's sons left the ark with Noah and received God's blessing and instructions to multiply and replenish the earth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noah's Wife And Sons' Wives">
  <data key="d0">Noah's Wife And Sons' Wives</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Noah's wife and his sons' wives left the ark with Noah and his sons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wind">
  <data key="d0">Wind</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The wind was made by God to pass over the earth and contribute to the abatement of the waters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fountains Of The Deep">
  <data key="d0">Fountains Of The Deep</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The fountains of the deep were stopped as the floodwaters receded.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121368</data>
