<node id="Reu">
  <data key="d0">Reu</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A descendant of Peleg who begat Serug and later had additional sons and daughters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serug">
  <data key="d0">Serug</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A descendant of Reu who begat Nahor and later had additional sons and daughters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nahor">
  <data key="d0">Nahor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A descendant of Serug who begat Terah and later had additional sons and daughters.&lt;SEP&gt;Nahor was Abraham's brother and the father of children born by Milcah.&lt;SEP&gt;Bethuel's father and Rebekah's grandfather.&lt;SEP&gt;Abraham's brother and the father of Bethuel.&lt;SEP&gt;Nahor is identified as Laban's father.&lt;SEP&gt;Nahor is identified as an ancestor associated with the God invoked by Laban.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Terah">
  <data key="d0">Terah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The father of Abram, Nahor, and Haran who traveled from Ur of the Chaldees and died in Haran.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abram">
  <data key="d0">Abram</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A patriarch who traveled to Canaan, received promises from the LORD, and built altars to the LORD.&lt;SEP&gt;A patriarch who travels through Canaan and Egypt, builds altars, journeys with Sarai and Lot, and receives promises from the LORD.&lt;SEP&gt;A patriarch who dwelt in the plain of Mamre, pursued the forces that captured Lot, rescued Lot and his possessions, and interacted with the kings of the region.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram is a patriarch who receives divine promises, believes in the LORD, performs the commanded animal preparation, and becomes the recipient of a covenant concerning land and descendants.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Haran (Person)">
  <data key="d0">Haran (Person)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The son of Terah, father of Lot, Milcah, and Iscah, who died in Ur of the Chaldees.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lot">
  <data key="d0">Lot</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The son of Haran who traveled with Terah and later accompanied Abram to Canaan.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram's relative and traveling companion who separates from Abram and chooses the plain of Jordan.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram's brother's son who dwelt in Sodom, was captured by Chedorlaomer's forces, and was rescued by Abram.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot receives the angels, offers them hospitality, confronts the men of Sodom, and is rescued from his house.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot is rescued from the destruction of the cities, enters Zoar, later dwells in a mountain cave, and fathers Moab and Benammi through his daughters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sarai">
  <data key="d0">Sarai</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Abram’s wife who traveled with Abram from Ur of the Chaldees to Canaan and was barren.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram's wife, described as very fair, whom Abram identifies as his sister during the journey to Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Sarai is Abram’s wife, a childless woman who gives Hagar to Abram and later treats Hagar harshly.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Milcah">
  <data key="d0">Milcah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The daughter of Haran and wife of Nahor.&lt;SEP&gt;Milcah bore eight children to Nahor, including Bethuel, and was identified as Abraham's sister-in-law through Nahor.&lt;SEP&gt;Bethuel's mother and Nahor's wife.&lt;SEP&gt;Nahor's wife and Bethuel's mother.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iscah">
  <data key="d0">Iscah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The daughter of Haran.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ur of the Chaldees">
  <data key="d0">Ur of the Chaldees</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The land of nativity from which Terah, Abram, Lot, and Sarai departed.&lt;SEP&gt;Ur of the Chaldees is the place from which the LORD brought Abram.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Haran (Location)">
  <data key="d0">Haran (Location)</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The settlement where Terah and his household dwelt after leaving Ur of the Chaldees and where Terah died.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sichem">
  <data key="d0">Sichem</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A place in Canaan through which Abram passed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Moreh">
  <data key="d0">Moreh</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The plain associated with the place of Sichem where Abram passed through Canaan.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bethel">
  <data key="d0">Bethel</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A place west of Abram’s tent when Abram camped on a mountain east of Bethel.&lt;SEP&gt;A place west of Abram's tent where Abram builds an altar and later returns to worship.&lt;SEP&gt;Bethel is the name Jacob gives to the place where Jacob sleeps, encounters the divine presence, and sets up a pillar.&lt;SEP&gt;Bethel is the place Jacob named after setting up and anointing a stone pillar.&lt;SEP&gt;Bethel was the place where Jacob anointed a pillar and made a vow to God.&lt;SEP&gt;Bethel is the place where Jacob is commanded to dwell and build an altar to God.&lt;SEP&gt;A place identified with Luz where God appeared to Jacob and where Jacob built an altar and set up a stone pillar.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hai">
  <data key="d0">Hai</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A place east of Abram’s tent when Abram camped on a mountain east of Bethel.&lt;SEP&gt;A place east of Abram's tent when Abram camps near Bethel.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canaanite">
  <data key="d0">Canaanite</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The people who were present in the land of Canaan when Abram passed through it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121371</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cattle">
  <data key="d0">Cattle</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Cattle are domesticated land animals and livestock described as being created according to their kinds. In the biblical account, they are included among the animals over which the serpent was cursed, and among the livestock associated with the people for whom Jabal is identified as the father. Herd animals representing their kinds were taken into Noah’s ark; cattle were therefore among the living creatures preserved through the flood and brought out afterward. They were also included among the domesticated animals covered by God’s covenant.

Cattle formed an important part of the wealth and pastoral life of Abram and Lot, whose herdsmen disputed because their shared land could not support both households’ livestock. They were among the animals that shepherds were instructed to gather and feed. In the account of Jacob and Laban, cattle included speckled, ringstraked, and grisled animals whose breeding contributed to Jacob’s increasing possessions. Laban’s cattle were tended by Jacob during six years of service, although Laban claimed them as his own. Jacob also owned cattle for which he made booths at Succoth.

During the famine in Egypt, cattle and other livestock—including herds, horses, flocks, and asses—were exchanged with Joseph in return for bread.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121372</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Land">
  <data key="d0">Land</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The territory that the LORD promises to Abram and Abram's seed, including the land viewed and traversed by Abram.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121372</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Covenant">
  <data key="d0">Covenant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Covenant refers to several distinct binding or sworn agreements described in biblical narratives.

The Noahic Covenant was established by God with Noah in connection with Noah’s survival in the ark. It extended to Noah’s descendants, living creatures, and the earth, and constituted a divine promise that another destructive flood would not occur.

A covenant between the LORD and Abram concerned the grant of land to Abram’s descendants. Related patriarchal covenants were described as everlasting agreements established by God with Isaac and Isaac’s descendants, and with Abraham, Abraham’s descendants, and the covenant community.

Covenant also denotes agreements between individuals. Abraham and Abimelech made a sworn agreement concerning mutual kindness and truthful dealings. Abimelech and his companions later proposed an agreement with Isaac that included a mutual pledge not to harm one another. Laban and Jacob established a covenant as a witness between them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plain Of Jordan">
  <data key="d0">Plain Of Jordan</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A well-watered region chosen by Lot, extending toward Sodom and compared with the garden of the LORD and the land of Egypt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jordan">
  <data key="d0">Jordan</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The geographic region associated with the well-watered plain chosen by Lot.&lt;SEP&gt;Jordan is the river that Jacob previously crossed with only a staff.&lt;SEP&gt;Jordan is the geographic reference beyond which the threshingfloor of Atad and Abelmizraim were located.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zoar">
  <data key="d0">Zoar</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A place near the plain of Jordan referenced in the comparison of the region to the land of Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Zoar is the small nearby city that Lot requests as a refuge, enters during the destruction, and later leaves because of fear.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Famine">
  <data key="d0">Famine</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A severe scarcity in the land that causes Abram to descend into Egypt temporarily.&lt;SEP&gt;A famine occurred in the land and prompted Isaac to go to Abimelech at Gerar.&lt;SEP&gt;The widespread scarcity that affected Egypt, Canaan, and other lands and drove people to Egypt for food.&lt;SEP&gt;The famine creates the need for Joseph's brothers to obtain and repeatedly purchase food.&lt;SEP&gt;The famine has lasted two years, with five additional years expected to lack planting and harvest.&lt;SEP&gt;The famine was a severe food shortage that caused Egypt and Canaan to lose bread, money, livestock, land, and freedom of service.&lt;SEP&gt;Famine was a severe food shortage affecting Canaan and Egypt, leaving the land without bread.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perizzites">
  <data key="d0">Perizzites</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A people dwelling in the land during the conflict between Abram's and Lot's herdsmen.&lt;SEP&gt;The Perizzites are a people listed among the nations associated with the land promised to Abram’s seed.&lt;SEP&gt;Perizzites are inhabitants of the land named with the Canaanites as potential opponents of Jacob and his household.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mountain">
  <data key="d0">Mountain</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A highland location east of Bethel where Abram pitches his tent and builds an altar.&lt;SEP&gt;The mountain is identified as a place of refuge, and Lot later dwells there with his daughters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharaoh's House">
  <data key="d0">Pharaoh's House</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The household or residence into which Sarai is taken after Pharaoh's princes commend her.&lt;SEP&gt;Pharaoh's House is the place where Joseph brought the money collected for corn from Egypt and Canaan.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Egyptian Princes">
  <data key="d0">Egyptian Princes</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Officials of Pharaoh who see Sarai, commend her before Pharaoh, and cause her to be taken into Pharaoh's house.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxen">
  <data key="d0">Oxen</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Cattle given to Abram as part of Pharaoh's favorable treatment of him because of Sarai.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacob reported possessing oxen when sending word to Esau.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asses">
  <data key="d0">Asses</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Donkeys given to Abram as part of Pharaoh's favorable treatment of him because of Sarai.&lt;SEP&gt;Donkeys belonging to Abraham and included among Abraham's possessions.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacob reported possessing asses when sending word to Esau.&lt;SEP&gt;The asses belonging to the men receive provender at Joseph's house.&lt;SEP&gt;The asses carry the corn that Joseph's brothers receive in Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;The asses carry the departing men and their sacks before the men return to the city.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Menservants">
  <data key="d0">Menservants</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Male servants given to Abram as part of Pharaoh's favorable treatment of him because of Sarai.&lt;SEP&gt;Male servants belonging to Abraham and accompanying Abraham's servant on the journey.&lt;SEP&gt;Menservants are male servants belonging to Jacob and included among Jacob's household and possessions.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacob reported possessing menservants when sending word to Esau.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-033</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maidservants">
  <data key="d0">Maidservants</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Female servants given to Abram as part of Pharaoh's favorable treatment of him because of Sarai.&lt;SEP&gt;Female servants belonging to Abraham and included among the possessions given to Isaac.&lt;SEP&gt;The maidservants had tents that Laban searched while looking for the household images.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Camels">
  <data key="d0">Camels</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Camels given to Abram as part of Pharaoh's favorable treatment of him because of Sarai.&lt;SEP&gt;The animals accompanying Abraham's servant and receiving water from Rebekah.&lt;SEP&gt;Ten camels belonging to Abraham are taken by Abraham's servant on the journey to Mesopotamia.&lt;SEP&gt;The camels accompanying Abraham's servant and receiving water from Rebekah.&lt;SEP&gt;Camels carried Jacob's sons and wives during Jacob's departure and carried the furniture in which Rachel hid the images.&lt;SEP&gt;Camels carried spicery, balm, and myrrh for the Ishmeelites traveling from Gilead to Egypt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plagues">
  <data key="d0">Plagues</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Great afflictions brought by the LORD upon Pharaoh and Pharaoh's household because of Sarai.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silver">
  <data key="d0">Silver</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A form of wealth in which Abram is described as being very rich.&lt;SEP&gt;A valuable material included among Abraham's possessions and given to Isaac.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Herdmen Of Abram">
  <data key="d0">Herdmen Of Abram</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The herdsmen responsible for Abram's cattle who engage in strife with Lot's herdsmen.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
