<node id="Hagar">
  <data key="d0">Hagar</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Hagar is an Egyptian handmaid of Sarai who becomes Abram’s wife, conceives a child by Abram, and flees after harsh treatment by Sarai.&lt;SEP&gt;A maid of Sarai and mother of Ishmael who fled from Sarai, encountered the angel of the LORD, and later bore Ishmael to Abraham.&lt;SEP&gt;Hagar is an Egyptian woman who bears a son to Abraham.&lt;SEP&gt;The Egyptian bondwoman of Abraham and mother of Hagar's son, who is sent away with her child.&lt;SEP&gt;Hagar is an Egyptian woman, Sarah's handmaid, and Ishmael's mother.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Angel of the LORD">
  <data key="d0">Angel of the LORD</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">The Angel of the LORD finds Hagar beside a fountain of water in the wilderness near Shur.&lt;SEP&gt;A divine messenger who found Hagar near a fountain, instructed her to return to Sarai, and announced promises concerning Ishmael.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shur">
  <data key="d0">Shur</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Shur is the wilderness route and location near the fountain where the Angel of the LORD finds Hagar.&lt;SEP&gt;A location on the way near the wilderness fountain where the angel of the LORD found Hagar.&lt;SEP&gt;Shur is a location between which Abraham dwells while journeying through the south country.&lt;SEP&gt;Shur is a location near Egypt included in the region where Ishmael's descendants dwelt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mamre">
  <data key="d0">Mamre</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The place whose plains contain Abraham's tent, where God appears and Abraham receives three visitors.&lt;SEP&gt;Mamre is one of the men who went with Abram and is designated to receive a portion of the recovered goods.&lt;SEP&gt;Mamre is the place before which the field and cave of Machpelah are situated.&lt;SEP&gt;Mamre is the place before which Machpelah and its field are located.&lt;SEP&gt;A place where Jacob came to Isaac.&lt;SEP&gt;Mamre is the place before which the Cave of Machpelah is situated.&lt;SEP&gt;Mamre is the place mentioned as the reference location near the field containing the cave of Machpelah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
