<node id="LORD">
  <data key="d0">LORD</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">LORD is portrayed as the divine judge, protector, and ruler of humanity and creation. The LORD received the cry of Abel’s blood, questioned Cain, warned him about sin, cursed him, and marked him for protection from being killed. The LORD judged humanity’s wickedness, intended to destroy humanity and other living creatures, yet showed grace to Noah. Observing the city and tower, the LORD confounded human language and scattered the people across the earth.

The LORD appeared to Abram, commanded him, promised land and descendants to his seed, received his worship, and brought plagues upon Pharaoh and his household. Abram built altars to the LORD and invoked him as the Most High God. The LORD is identified as the Most High, possessor of heaven and earth, speaker to Abram, giver of the land, judge of nations, and maker of a covenant with him. The LORD sent angels to destroy Sodom and Gomorrah, destroyed the cities with brimstone and fire, and showed mercy to Lot. The LORD visited Sarah and fulfilled the promise of Isaac’s birth, and was invoked in the angel’s declaration and in the naming of the mountain associated with divine provision.

The LORD guided Abraham’s servant, prospered his journey, appointed Rebekah for Isaac, and was worshiped and invoked as the God of heaven and earth, who blessed Abraham and sent an angel before the servant. The LORD appeared to Isaac, identified himself as the God of Abraham, instructed Isaac to remain in the land, promised blessings and nations to his descendants, blessed his agricultural work and the field whose fragrance Isaac associated with his son, and answered Isaac’s petition concerning Rebekah as well as Rebekah’s inquiry. Jacob declared that the LORD would be his God after his peaceful return to his father’s house and identified the LORD as the source of salvation. The LORD remained with Joseph, showed him mercy, caused his work to prosper, and blessed the Egyptian household for Joseph’s sake.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
