<node id="Fountain of Water">
  <data key="d0">Fountain of Water</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The fountain of water in the wilderness near the way to Shur is where the Angel of the LORD finds Hagar.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121376</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canaanites">
  <data key="d0">Canaanites</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Canaanites were a people descended from Canaan who inhabited the land extending from Sidon to Lasha. They are listed among the nations associated with the territory promised to Abram’s descendants and are described as dwelling in the land where Abraham lived.

The Canaanites were present during the dispute between Abram’s and Lot’s herdsmen. Because Abraham lived among them, he prohibited his servant from taking a wife for Isaac from the Canaanite population, indicating a clear distinction between Abraham’s family and the people of the land.

Later, Jacob feared that the Canaanites and other inhabitants of the region would gather against him after the attack on Shechem. The Canaanites also witnessed the mourning at the threshing floor of Atad, recognizing it as an exceptionally grievous mourning conducted by the Egyptians.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ishmael">
  <data key="d0">Ishmael</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Abraham's son who is blessed by God, promised descendants and a great nation, and is circumcised at thirteen years of age.&lt;SEP&gt;The son of Abraham and Hagar, whose birth was announced by the angel of the LORD and who was blessed by God.&lt;SEP&gt;Ishmael is Abraham and Hagar's son and the father of twelve princes.&lt;SEP&gt;Ishmael is Abraham's son and the father of Mahalath.&lt;SEP&gt;The father of Bashemath and the grandfather of Nebajoth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canaan">
  <data key="d0">Canaan</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Canaan refers both to a biblical person and to the land associated with his descendants. Canaan, the son of Ham, was cursed to become a “servant of servants” to his brethren. He was identified as the father of Sidon, Heth, and several Canaanite peoples.

Canaan also denotes the land to which Abram traveled with Sarai and Lot, and which the LORD promised to Abram’s seed and to Abraham’s descendants as an everlasting possession. Abram lived there after separating from Lot. The land included Kirjatharba, identified as Hebron, the city of Shechem, and the field and Cave of Machpelah, including the burial place of Joseph’s father. It was also the land where Rachel died.

In the accounts of Isaac’s and Jacob’s families, Canaan was the region whose daughters Isaac forbade Jacob and Esau to marry. Jacob, Isaac, Esau, and Esau’s family lived in or traveled through it; Esau’s sons were born there and Esau acquired his possessions there. Jacob dwelt in Canaan and intended to return there to his father Isaac.

During the famine, Canaan was the family’s former homeland and a land severely affected by scarcity. Jacob and his sons lived there, and Joseph’s brothers returned there with money and repeatedly traveled from it to obtain grain. Pharaoh instructed them to return to Canaan and bring Jacob and their households to Egypt, from which Jacob and his family ultimately departed. Canaan therefore represents both the ancestral homeland and the divinely promised inheritance of Abraham’s descendants.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Circumcision">
  <data key="d0">Circumcision</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A ritual procedure involving the flesh of the foreskin, performed on Abraham, Ishmael, and the males of Abraham's household.&lt;SEP&gt;A required bodily rite designated as the token of God's covenant and required for male children among Abraham's descendants and household.&lt;SEP&gt;Circumcision is the condition imposed by Jacob's sons for marriage alliances and shared residence, and every male of Shechem's city undergoes it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-035</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beerlahairoi">
  <data key="d0">Beerlahairoi</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A well located between Kadesh and Bered.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bered">
  <data key="d0">Bered</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A location identified as one endpoint of the area between which Beerlahairoi lies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three Men">
  <data key="d0">Three Men</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Three visitors who stand near Abraham at Mamre, receive hospitality, ask about Sarah, and look toward Sodom.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abraham's Household">
  <data key="d0">Abraham's Household</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The household under Abraham's authority, including males born in the household and males bought with money, whose members are commanded to follow the way of the LORD and undergo circumcision.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Twelve Princes">
  <data key="d0">Twelve Princes</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The twelve rulers whom God promises Ishmael will beget as part of Ishmael's multiplication and rise as a great nation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nations of the Earth">
  <data key="d0">Nations of the Earth</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The collective nations that God says will be blessed through Abraham.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Way of the LORD">
  <data key="d0">Way of the LORD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The divinely directed way that Abraham's children and household are expected to keep by practicing justice and judgment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Justice and Judgment">
  <data key="d0">Justice and Judgment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ethical conduct that Abraham's children and household are instructed to practice while keeping the way of the LORD.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="The LORD">
  <data key="d0">The LORD</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The LORD is the divine judge who hears the cry concerning Sodom and Gomorrah, investigates wrongdoing, offers conditional mercy, and sends angels to destroy Sodom.&lt;SEP&gt;The LORD is the divine speaker who identifies as the God of Abraham and Isaac, promises land and descendants to Jacob, and pledges protection.&lt;SEP&gt;The LORD slew Er and Onan after their conduct was judged wicked or displeasing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Righteous">
  <data key="d0">Righteous</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The righteous are inhabitants of Sodom whose presence is presented as the basis for sparing the city.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wicked">
  <data key="d0">Wicked</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The wicked are inhabitants whose fate Abraham asks the LORD not to impose on the righteous.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Two Angels">
  <data key="d0">Two Angels</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Two angels come to Sodom, stay with Lot, protect Lot from the men at his door, and announce the destruction of the city.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lot's House">
  <data key="d0">Lot's House</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Lot's house is the dwelling where Lot hosts the angels and from which the angels rescue Lot.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Men of Sodom">
  <data key="d0">Men of Sodom</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The men of Sodom surround Lot's house, demand that the visiting men be brought out, and attempt to force entry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lot's Daughters">
  <data key="d0">Lot's Daughters</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lot's daughters are members of Lot's household whom Lot identifies as having not known man.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lot's Sons-in-Law">
  <data key="d0">Lot's Sons-in-Law</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lot's sons-in-law are household members whom the angels instruct Lot to bring out of the place.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot's sons-in-law are married to Lot's daughters and reject Lot's warning about the destruction of the city.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lot's Sons">
  <data key="d0">Lot's Sons</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lot's sons are members of Lot's household whom the angels instruct Lot to bring out of Sodom.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lot's Family">
  <data key="d0">Lot's Family</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lot's family consists of Lot's sons-in-law, sons, daughters, and other household members whom the angels instruct Lot to remove from Sodom.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lot's Wife">
  <data key="d0">Lot's Wife</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lot's wife escapes the city with Lot but looks back and becomes a pillar of salt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lot's Firstborn Daughter">
  <data key="d0">Lot's Firstborn Daughter</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lot's firstborn daughter conspires with her younger sister, lies with Lot while he is intoxicated, and bears Moab.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lot's Younger Daughter">
  <data key="d0">Lot's Younger Daughter</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lot's younger daughter conspires with her firstborn sister, lies with Lot while he is intoxicated, and bears Benammi.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Angels">
  <data key="d0">Angels</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">The angels warn Lot, hasten his departure, take hold of Lot and his family, and bring them outside the city.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plain">
  <data key="d0">Plain</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The plain surrounding the cities is destroyed along with the cities and their inhabitants.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cave">
  <data key="d0">Cave</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The cave is the dwelling place where Lot lives with his two daughters after leaving Zoar.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pillar of Salt">
  <data key="d0">Pillar of Salt</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The pillar of salt is the form Lot's wife assumes after looking back during the escape.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Moab">
  <data key="d0">Moab</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Moab is the son born to Lot's firstborn daughter and is identified as the father of the Moabites.&lt;SEP&gt;Moab is identified as the son of the firstborn and as the father of the Moabites.&lt;SEP&gt;Moab is the region where Hadad defeated Midian.&lt;SEP&gt;Moab was the location of the field where Hadad smote Midian.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Moabites">
  <data key="d0">Moabites</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Moabites are the people identified as descendants of Moab.&lt;SEP&gt;The Moabites are identified as descendants of Moab.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Benammi">
  <data key="d0">Benammi</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Benammi is the son born to Lot's younger daughter and is identified as the father of the children of Ammon.&lt;SEP&gt;Benammi is identified as the son of the younger daughter and as the father of the children of Ammon.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children of Ammon">
  <data key="d0">Children of Ammon</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The children of Ammon are identified as descendants of Benammi.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="South Country">
  <data key="d0">South Country</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The south country is the region toward which Abraham journeys after the events involving Lot and the destroyed cities.&lt;SEP&gt;The south country is the region toward which Abraham journeys before dwelling between Kadesh and Shur.&lt;SEP&gt;The southern region where Isaac dwells.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brimstone">
  <data key="d0">Brimstone</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Brimstone is a substance rained upon Sodom and Gomorrah during their destruction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fire">
  <data key="d0">Fire</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fire is rained from heaven upon Sodom and Gomorrah during their destruction.&lt;SEP&gt;Fire carried by Abraham for the burnt offering.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smoke">
  <data key="d0">Smoke</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Smoke rises from the land of the plain after the destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah and is compared to smoke from a furnace.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children Of Ammon">
  <data key="d0">Children Of Ammon</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The children of Ammon are the people identified as descendants of Benammi.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abimelech">
  <data key="d0">Abimelech</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Abimelech is the king of Gerar who takes Sarah, receives a warning from God, restores Sarah, and gives gifts to Abraham.&lt;SEP&gt;A ruler who asks Abraham for an oath, receives animals from Abraham, and makes a covenant with Abraham.&lt;SEP&gt;Abimelech is king of the Philistines who received Isaac at Gerar, confronted Isaac about Rebekah, protected the household, and later told Isaac to leave.&lt;SEP&gt;A ruler from Gerar who visited Isaac with Ahuzzath and Phichol to establish an oath and covenant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hagar's Son">
  <data key="d0">Hagar's Son</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The son of Hagar and Abraham who is cast out with Hagar, rescued by God, grows in the wilderness, and becomes an archer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Angel of God">
  <data key="d0">Angel of God</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">A heavenly messenger who calls to Hagar and tells Hagar not to fear.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phichol">
  <data key="d0">Phichol</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The chief captain of Abimelech's host who accompanies Abimelech in dealings with Abraham.&lt;SEP&gt;The chief captain of Abimelech's army who accompanied Abimelech to Isaac.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beersheba">
  <data key="d0">Beersheba</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The place associated with Hagar's wilderness journey, Abraham's well, and the covenant between Abraham and Abimelech.&lt;SEP&gt;Beersheba was the destination to which Abraham returned and the place where Abraham dwelt.&lt;SEP&gt;A place to which Isaac traveled and the city associated with the name Shebah.&lt;SEP&gt;Beersheba is the place from which Jacob departs toward Haran.&lt;SEP&gt;Beersheba is the place where Jacob offers sacrifices and begins the journey to Egypt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wilderness of Paran">
  <data key="d0">Wilderness of Paran</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The wilderness where Hagar's son dwells and grows.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Land of the Philistines">
  <data key="d0">Land of the Philistines</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The land to which Abimelech and Phichol return and where Abraham sojourns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Well of Water">
  <data key="d0">Well of Water</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A water source associated with Hagar's rescue and a dispute between Abraham and Abimelech's servants.&lt;SEP&gt;The well of water outside the City of Nahor is where Abraham's servant stops with the camels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
