<node id="Sons Of Heth">
  <data key="d0">Sons Of Heth</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The sons of Heth were local people who responded to Abraham's request for a burial place.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ephron">
  <data key="d0">Ephron</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ephron was the son of Zohar and the person Abraham asked the sons of Heth to approach regarding a burial place.&lt;SEP&gt;Ephron the Hittite owns the field and cave of Machpelah and negotiates their transfer to Abraham.&lt;SEP&gt;Ephron is the son of Zohar and the owner associated with the field containing Machpelah.&lt;SEP&gt;Ephron is identified as a Hittite whose field and cave Abraham purchased as a burial possession.&lt;SEP&gt;Ephron is identified as the Hittite associated with the field containing the cave of Machpelah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zohar">
  <data key="d0">Zohar</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zohar was the father of Ephron.&lt;SEP&gt;Zohar is Ephron's father.&lt;SEP&gt;Zohar is a son of Simeon.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Children of Heth">
  <data key="d0">Children of Heth</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The children of Heth are a people among whom Ephron dwells and before whom the property transaction is witnessed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cave of Machpelah">
  <data key="d0">Cave of Machpelah</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cave of Machpelah is a burial cave in Ephron's field where Abraham buries Sarah.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cave of Machpelah is a burial cave in the field before Mamre in Canaan.&lt;SEP&gt;The cave of Machpelah in Canaan served as Joseph's father's burial place.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Field of Ephron">
  <data key="d0">Field of Ephron</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Field of Ephron contains the Cave of Machpelah, trees, and surrounding borders and becomes Abraham's possession.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abraham's Eldest Servant">
  <data key="d0">Abraham's Eldest Servant</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Abraham's eldest servant rules over Abraham's possessions and travels to find a wife for Isaac.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Angel">
  <data key="d0">Angel</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">A heavenly messenger whom the LORD promises to send with Abraham's servant.&lt;SEP&gt;The angel is described as being sent by the LORD before Abraham's servant.&lt;SEP&gt;The Angel is described as redeeming Jacob from evil and being invoked to bless Ephraim and Manasseh.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mesopotamia">
  <data key="d0">Mesopotamia</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Mesopotamia is the region to which Abraham's servant travels in search of a wife for Isaac.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="City of Nahor">
  <data key="d0">City of Nahor</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The City of Nahor is the destination in Mesopotamia reached by Abraham's servant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Four Hundred Shekels of Silver">
  <data key="d0">Four Hundred Shekels of Silver</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Four hundred shekels of silver are the stated value paid by Abraham to Ephron for the field and cave.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abraham's Servant">
  <data key="d0">Abraham's Servant</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Abraham's unnamed servant who travels to Abraham's kindred, identifies Rebekah, negotiates her departure, and brings her to Isaac.&lt;SEP&gt;An unnamed servant of Abraham who travels to seek a wife for Isaac, prays for divine guidance, meets Rebekah, and reports his mission to her family.&lt;SEP&gt;Abraham's servant met Rebekah, identified Isaac as the servant's master, and reported the servant's actions to Isaac.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121380</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Egyptians">
  <data key="d0">Egyptians</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Egyptians are the people of Egypt portrayed in several episodes involving Abraham’s family and Joseph’s administration. They observe Sarai’s beauty and report her to Pharaoh. They also maintain separate dining customs, eating apart from the Hebrews because eating bread with Hebrews is regarded as an abomination.

During the famine, the Egyptians seek bread from Pharaoh and purchase food from Joseph. As the famine continues, they exchange their livestock for food and ultimately sell their fields to Joseph. The Egyptians also hear Joseph weeping after he reveals his identity to his brothers.

Following Israel’s death, the Egyptians mourn him for seventy days and participate in the mourning observed at the threshing floor of Atad.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121384</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Well">
  <data key="d0">Well</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A water well where Rebekah draws water and where Abraham's servant waits for a sign concerning Isaac's future wife.&lt;SEP&gt;A dug structure from which water was obtained and over which people sometimes strove.&lt;SEP&gt;The well was a water source in a field, covered by a large stone and used to water flocks.</data>
