<node id="Joseph's Dreams">
  <data key="d0">Joseph's Dreams</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph's dreams depicted his sheaf receiving obeisance from other sheaves and the sun, moon, and eleven stars bowing to him.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph's dreams were referenced by Joseph's brothers when they discussed Joseph's fate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph's Brothers">
  <data key="d0">Joseph's Brothers</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph's brothers conspired against Joseph, stripped Joseph of his coat, cast Joseph into a pit, and agreed to sell Joseph.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph's brothers travel to Egypt for corn, are accused of spying, carry provisions home, and acknowledge guilt concerning Joseph.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph's brothers are the men who dine with Joseph, travel with Benjamin, discover the silver cup, and return to Joseph's house.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph's brothers feared retaliation, requested forgiveness, served Joseph, and participated in the family's movements and burial activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ishmeelites">
  <data key="d0">Ishmeelites</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Ishmeelites traveled from Gilead toward Egypt with camels carrying spicery, balm, and myrrh, and purchased Joseph.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ishmeelites transported Joseph to Egypt and sold Joseph to Potiphar.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Midianites">
  <data key="d0">Midianites</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Midianites drew Joseph out of the pit, sold Joseph to the Ishmeelites, and later sold Joseph into Egypt to Potiphar.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gilead">
  <data key="d0">Gilead</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Gilead was the place from which the Ishmeelites traveled toward Egypt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A Pit In The Wilderness">
  <data key="d0">A Pit In The Wilderness</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">A pit in the wilderness was proposed by Reuben and used to confine Joseph; the pit was empty and contained no water.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph's Coat">
  <data key="d0">Joseph's Coat</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph's coat was a coat of many colours that Joseph's brothers removed, dipped in goat blood, and presented to Jacob.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Twenty Pieces Of Silver">
  <data key="d0">Twenty Pieces Of Silver</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Twenty pieces of silver were the stated payment given to the Midianites for Joseph.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potiphar">
  <data key="d0">Potiphar</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Potiphar was an officer of Pharaoh and captain of the guard who received Joseph after the Midianites sold Joseph into Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Potiphar is an Egyptian officer of Pharaoh and captain of the guard who bought Joseph and placed Joseph over his household.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hirah">
  <data key="d0">Hirah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Hirah was an Adullamite with whom Judah stayed after departing from his brothers.&lt;SEP&gt;Hirah is Judah's friend, an Adullamite, who accompanied Judah to Timnath and attempted to deliver a kid and recover Judah's pledge.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Er">
  <data key="d0">Er</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Er was Judah's firstborn son and Tamar's husband who was wicked in the sight of the LORD and was slain by the LORD.&lt;SEP&gt;Er is a son of Judah who died in the land of Canaan.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Onan">
  <data key="d0">Onan</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Onan was Judah's son who was instructed to marry Tamar, refused to provide offspring for his brother, and was slain by the LORD.&lt;SEP&gt;Onan is a son of Judah who died in the land of Canaan.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shelah">
  <data key="d0">Shelah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Shelah was Judah's son, born to Shuah's daughter, whom Judah intended Tamar to await until Shelah matured.&lt;SEP&gt;Shelah is Judah's son whom Tamar was expected to marry after reaching maturity.&lt;SEP&gt;Shelah is a son of Judah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tamar">
  <data key="d0">Tamar</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Tamar was Er's wife and Judah's daughter-in-law who was instructed to remain a widow at her father's house.&lt;SEP&gt;Tamar is Judah's daughter-in-law who lived in her father's house as a widow, disguised herself, conceived twins by Judah, and became the mother of Pharez and Zarah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chezib">
  <data key="d0">Chezib</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Chezib was the place where Shuah's daughter was when she gave birth to Shelah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Timnath">
  <data key="d0">Timnath</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Timnath was the destination of Judah's journey to his sheepshearers after Shuah's daughter died.&lt;SEP&gt;Timnath is the destination where Judah went to shear sheep and where Tamar positioned herself beside the road.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Evil Beast">
  <data key="d0">Evil Beast</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">An evil beast was presented by Joseph's brothers as a false explanation for Joseph's supposed death.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spicery">
  <data key="d0">Spicery</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Spicery was cargo carried by the Ishmeelites on camels while traveling toward Egypt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Balm">
  <data key="d0">Balm</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Balm was cargo carried by the Ishmeelites on camels while traveling toward Egypt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Myrrh">
  <data key="d0">Myrrh</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Myrrh was cargo carried by the Ishmeelites on camels while traveling toward Egypt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sackcloth">
  <data key="d0">Sackcloth</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Sackcloth was worn by Jacob around his loins as part of his mourning for Joseph.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kid">
  <data key="d0">Kid</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">The kid is a young goat promised by Judah to Tamar as payment and sent through Hirah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Signet">
  <data key="d0">Signet</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The signet is one of the personal objects Judah gave Tamar as a pledge.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Staff">
  <data key="d0">Staff</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The staff is a personal object Judah gave Tamar as part of his pledge.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharez">
  <data key="d0">Pharez</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharez is one of Tamar's twin sons who was born before the brother marked by the scarlet thread.&lt;SEP&gt;Pharez is a son of Judah and the father of Hezron and Hamul.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zarah">
  <data key="d0">Zarah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zarah is one of Tamar's twin sons who was born after Pharez and had the scarlet thread placed on his hand.&lt;SEP&gt;Zarah is a son of Judah.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scarlet Thread">
  <data key="d0">Scarlet Thread</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The scarlet thread was tied to the hand of the child who appeared to come out first during Tamar's labor.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Judah's Wife">
  <data key="d0">Judah's Wife</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Judah's Wife was the daughter of Shuah and died before Judah traveled to Timnath.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Widow's Garments">
  <data key="d0">Widow's Garments</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Widow's garments were worn by Tamar, removed during her disguise, and put on again afterward.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Veil">
  <data key="d0">Veil</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The veil covered Tamar's face during her encounter with Judah and was later put aside.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Midwife">
  <data key="d0">Midwife</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The midwife attended Tamar during her labor and tied a scarlet thread to the hand of the child who appeared to emerge first.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph's Master">
  <data key="d0">Joseph's Master</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph's master entrusts the household and possessions to Joseph, becomes angry after hearing his wife's accusation, and sends Joseph to prison.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph's Master's Wife">
  <data key="d0">Joseph's Master's Wife</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph's master's wife repeatedly attempts to have Joseph lie with her, seizes Joseph's garment, and accuses Joseph of wrongdoing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Egyptian's House">
  <data key="d0">Egyptian's House</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The Egyptian's house is the household managed by Joseph and blessed by the LORD for Joseph's sake.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph's Garment">
  <data key="d0">Joseph's Garment</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph's garment is seized by Joseph's master's wife and left behind when Joseph flees.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prison">
  <data key="d0">Prison</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The prison is where Joseph is confined and where the king's prisoners, the chief butler, and the chief baker are held.&lt;SEP&gt;The prison is the place where Joseph's brothers are held and where Simeon is bound.&lt;SEP&gt;The place where Joseph confined his brethren while testing the truth of their account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-045</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Keeper of the Prison">
  <data key="d0">Keeper of the Prison</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The keeper of the prison oversees the prisoners and entrusts their management and prison duties to Joseph.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prisoners">
  <data key="d0">Prisoners</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The prisoners are people confined in the prison and placed under Joseph's responsibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chief Butler">
  <data key="d0">Chief Butler</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The chief butler is Pharaoh's officer who offends Pharaoh, is imprisoned, dreams a dream, and tells the dream to Joseph.&lt;SEP&gt;Pharaoh's butler who dreamed of a vine and a cup, received Joseph's interpretation, was restored to office, and later remembered Joseph before Pharaoh.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chief Baker">
  <data key="d0">Chief Baker</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The chief baker is Pharaoh's officer who offends Pharaoh, is imprisoned, and dreams a dream.&lt;SEP&gt;Pharaoh's baker who dreamed of three baskets and received Joseph's interpretation that he would be hanged.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Captain of the Guard">
  <data key="d0">Captain of the Guard</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The captain of the guard places the chief butler and chief baker in ward and charges Joseph with them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dream">
  <data key="d0">Dream</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A dream is an experience reported by the chief butler and chief baker for which no interpreter is initially available.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vine">
  <data key="d0">Vine</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">A vine appears before the chief butler in his dream.&lt;SEP&gt;A vine in the chief butler's dream that had three branches, blossoms, and ripe grape clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Egyptian">
  <data key="d0">Egyptian</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Egyptian owns the house in which Joseph serves as overseer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Land Of The Hebrews">
  <data key="d0">Land Of The Hebrews</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The land from which Joseph said he had been stolen away.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dungeon">
  <data key="d0">Dungeon</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The place where Joseph was confined before Pharaoh summoned him.&lt;SEP&gt;The dungeon is the place from which Pharaoh summons Joseph.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dreams">
  <data key="d0">Dreams</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Dream experiences described by the chief butler, the chief baker, Pharaoh, and Joseph's account of interpreting dreams.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dream Interpretations">
  <data key="d0">Dream Interpretations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Explanations of dream symbols, attributed by Joseph to God and applied to the dreams of the butler, baker, and Pharaoh.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharaoh's Cup">
  <data key="d0">Pharaoh's Cup</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The cup held by the chief butler, filled with pressed grapes and delivered into Pharaoh's hand.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grapes">
  <data key="d0">Grapes</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ripe fruit from the dream vine that the chief butler pressed into Pharaoh's cup.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three Branches">
  <data key="d0">Three Branches</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The three branches in the chief butler's dream, interpreted by Joseph as three days.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three Baskets">
  <data key="d0">Three Baskets</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Three white baskets in the chief baker's dream, with the uppermost basket containing baked food for Pharaoh.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Birds">
  <data key="d0">Birds</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Birds that ate the baked food from the chief baker's basket and were prophesied to eat the baker's flesh.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tree">
  <data key="d0">Tree</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The tree on which Joseph interpreted that the chief baker would be hanged.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Well-Favoured Kine">
  <data key="d0">Well-Favoured Kine</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven fat cattle in Pharaoh's dream that fed in a meadow before being eaten by seven ill-favoured cattle.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ill-Favoured Kine">
  <data key="d0">Ill-Favoured Kine</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven lean cattle in Pharaoh's dream that emerged after the well-favoured cattle and devoured them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meadow">
  <data key="d0">Meadow</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The grassy place where the seven well-favoured cattle fed in Pharaoh's dream.&lt;SEP&gt;The meadow is the place where the seven fat cattle feed in Pharaoh’s dream.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rank Ears Of Corn">
  <data key="d0">Rank Ears Of Corn</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven full ears of corn growing on one stalk in Pharaoh's dream.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thin Ears Of Corn">
  <data key="d0">Thin Ears Of Corn</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven thin ears blasted by the east wind that devoured the seven rank ears in Pharaoh's dream.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magicians Of Egypt">
  <data key="d0">Magicians Of Egypt</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A group summoned by Pharaoh to interpret his dreams, none of whom could interpret them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wise Men Of Egypt">
  <data key="d0">Wise Men Of Egypt</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A group summoned by Pharaoh alongside the magicians to interpret his dreams, without success.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Captain Of The Guard">
  <data key="d0">Captain Of The Guard</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The guard officer to whom Joseph was a servant and whose house held Joseph and the chief butler and baker in ward.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharaoh's Birthday">
  <data key="d0">Pharaoh's Birthday</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The third day on which Pharaoh held a feast and lifted up the heads of the chief butler and chief baker.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three Days">
  <data key="d0">Three Days</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The time period represented by the three branches in the chief butler's dream and the three baskets in the chief baker's dream.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Two Full Years">
  <data key="d0">Two Full Years</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The period that passed before Pharaoh dreamed and Joseph was summoned from the dungeon.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Captain Of The Guard's House">
  <data key="d0">Captain Of The Guard's House</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The house where the chief butler, the chief baker, and Joseph were held in ward under the captain of the guard.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharaohs Dream">
  <data key="d0">Pharaohs Dream</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharaoh’s doubled dream contains seven fat cattle, seven lean cattle, seven good ears, and seven thin ears that symbolize future years.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seven Fat Cattle">
  <data key="d0">Seven Fat Cattle</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven well-favoured, fat cattle emerge from the river and symbolize seven years of plenty.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seven Lean Cattle">
  <data key="d0">Seven Lean Cattle</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven ill-favoured, lean cattle emerge after the fat cattle and symbolize seven years of famine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seven Good Ears">
  <data key="d0">Seven Good Ears</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven full and good ears growing on one stalk symbolize seven years of plenty.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seven Thin Ears">
  <data key="d0">Seven Thin Ears</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven withered, thin ears blasted by the east wind symbolize seven years of famine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seven Years of Plenty">
  <data key="d0">Seven Years of Plenty</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven years of exceptional agricultural abundance are foretold throughout Egypt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seven Years of Famine">
  <data key="d0">Seven Years of Famine</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven years of severe famine are foretold after the years of plenty, threatening Egypt with ruin.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magicians">
  <data key="d0">Magicians</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharaoh’s magicians hear the dream but cannot interpret or explain it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spirit of God">
  <data key="d0">Spirit of God</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Spirit of God is identified by Pharaoh as present in Joseph.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asenath">
  <data key="d0">Asenath</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Asenath becomes Joseph’s wife and is the daughter of Potipherah, priest of On.&lt;SEP&gt;The daughter of Potipherah and wife of Joseph who bore Joseph two sons.&lt;SEP&gt;Asenath is the daughter of Potipherah and bears Manasseh and Ephraim to Joseph in Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Asenath was the daughter of Potipherah and the mother of Manasseh and Ephraim.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Potipherah">
  <data key="d0">Potipherah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Potipherah is identified as the priest of On and the father of Asenath.&lt;SEP&gt;The priest of On and father of Asenath.&lt;SEP&gt;Potipherah is the priest of On and the father of Asenath.&lt;SEP&gt;Potipherah was a priest of On and the father of Asenath.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="On">
  <data key="d0">On</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">On is the place associated with Potipherah’s priesthood.&lt;SEP&gt;The place associated with Potipherah's priesthood.&lt;SEP&gt;On is the place associated with Potipherah's priesthood.&lt;SEP&gt;On was the place associated with Potipherah's priesthood.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pharaohs Ring">
  <data key="d0">Pharaohs Ring</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharaoh’s ring is transferred to Joseph as a sign of delegated authority.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Second Chariot">
  <data key="d0">Second Chariot</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Pharaoh’s second chariot carries Joseph during Joseph’s public elevation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zaphnathpaaneah">
  <data key="d0">Zaphnathpaaneah</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zaphnathpaaneah is the name Pharaoh gives Joseph after appointing Joseph over Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;The name Pharaoh gave to Joseph.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Officers">
  <data key="d0">Officers</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The officers are officials whom Pharaoh is instructed to appoint over Egypt during the years of plenty.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Food Stores">
  <data key="d0">Food Stores</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Food stores consist of food and corn gathered during the years of plenty and kept for the famine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manasseh">
  <data key="d0">Manasseh</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The first son born to Joseph and Asenath.&lt;SEP&gt;Manasseh is a son born to Joseph and Asenath in Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Manasseh was Joseph's son, born to Joseph in Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Manasseh is Joseph's son who accompanied Joseph when Joseph visited the sick Jacob.&lt;SEP&gt;Manasseh is Joseph's firstborn son and receives a blessing from Jacob, although Ephraim is placed before him.&lt;SEP&gt;Manasseh is identified as the father of Machir.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ephraim">
  <data key="d0">Ephraim</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The second son born to Joseph and Asenath.&lt;SEP&gt;Ephraim is a son born to Joseph and Asenath in Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Ephraim was Joseph's son, born to Joseph in Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Ephraim is Joseph's son who accompanied Joseph when Joseph visited the sick Jacob.&lt;SEP&gt;Ephraim is Joseph's younger son and is blessed by Jacob with precedence over Manasseh.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seven Plenteous Years">
  <data key="d0">Seven Plenteous Years</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The seven-year period in which Egypt produced abundant harvests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seven Years of Dearth">
  <data key="d0">Seven Years of Dearth</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The seven-year period of scarcity that followed the plentiful years.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Storehouses">
  <data key="d0">Storehouses</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage facilities in which Joseph placed the food gathered from Egypt's harvests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph's Brethren">
  <data key="d0">Joseph's Brethren</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph's brothers who traveled from Canaan to Egypt to purchase food and bowed before Joseph.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph's brethren are the brothers who sold Joseph into Egypt and later came to Egypt during the famine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-048</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jacob (Israel)">
  <data key="d0">Jacob (Israel)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Jacob, also called Israel, is the brothers' father who receives their report, fears the loss of his sons, and initially refuses to send Benjamin.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-045</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Money">
  <data key="d0">Money</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Money is placed in the brothers' sacks by Joseph and later discovered by the brothers and Jacob.&lt;SEP&gt;The money consists of the original payment returned in the men's sacks and additional money brought to buy food.&lt;SEP&gt;Money was used to purchase corn and later became unavailable to the Egyptians and Canaanites during the famine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interpreter">
  <data key="d0">Interpreter</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The interpreter conveys Joseph's words to his brothers, who do not realize that Joseph understands their conversation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-045</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inn">
  <data key="d0">Inn</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The inn is the stopping place where one of Joseph's brothers discovers money in a sack while obtaining provender for an ass.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-045</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph's House">
  <data key="d0">Joseph's House</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph's house is the residence where Joseph's brothers are brought, receive hospitality, and dine.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph's house is the place where Joseph remains and where Judah and his brothers return after the silver cup is discovered.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hebrews">
  <data key="d0">Hebrews</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Hebrews are the people identified as eating separately from the Egyptians.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hebrews are the people whose dining arrangements are kept separate from the Egyptians.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Israel's Sons">
  <data key="d0">Israel's Sons</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Israel's sons are the group of brothers who travel to Egypt with Benjamin to buy food and appear before Joseph.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-046</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ruler of Joseph's House">
  <data key="d0">Ruler of Joseph's House</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The ruler of Joseph's house receives Joseph's order to bring the men home and prepare a meal.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-046</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Steward of Joseph's House">
  <data key="d0">Steward of Joseph's House</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The steward of Joseph's house speaks with the men at the door, reassures them about the returned money, and brings Simeon out to them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-046</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph's Steward">
  <data key="d0">Joseph's Steward</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph's steward is the household servant commanded to fill the men's sacks, place money and the silver cup in a sack, pursue the men, and search the sacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silver Cup">
  <data key="d0">Silver Cup</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The silver cup is Joseph's drinking and divining vessel that the steward places in Benjamin's sack.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Benjamin's Sack">
  <data key="d0">Benjamin's Sack</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Benjamin's sack is the container in which Joseph's silver cup is found.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Benjamin's Father">
  <data key="d0">Benjamin's Father</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Benjamin's father is an old man who loves Benjamin and is described as unable to endure Benjamin's departure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joseph's Father">
  <data key="d0">Joseph's Father</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Joseph's father is an unnamed father whose life is described as bound up with Benjamin's life and who is invited to move to Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph's father commanded Joseph to bury him in the land of Canaan and was later buried there.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="House of Pharaoh">
  <data key="d0">House of Pharaoh</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The house of Pharaoh hears that Joseph's brethren have arrived, and the news pleases Pharaoh and his servants.&lt;SEP&gt;The House of Pharaoh is the royal household to which Joseph speaks about Jacob’s burial request.&lt;SEP&gt;The house of Pharaoh was addressed by Joseph when Joseph sought permission to bury Joseph's father.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Goshen">
  <data key="d0">Goshen</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Goshen is the Egyptian land designated as a dwelling place for Joseph's father, descendants, flocks, herds, and possessions.&lt;SEP&gt;Goshen was the Egyptian land where Jacob's family settled with Pharaoh's permission.&lt;SEP&gt;Goshen is the country in Egypt where Israel dwelt and possessed land.&lt;SEP&gt;Goshen is the Egyptian land where the younger family members, flocks, and herds remained during the burial journey.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wagons">
  <data key="d0">Wagons</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Wagons are vehicles from Egypt that Pharaoh commands Joseph's brethren to take for their children and wives.&lt;SEP&gt;Wagons are vehicles sent by Pharaoh and provided by Joseph to transport Jacob, his household, and their possessions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phallu">
  <data key="d0">Phallu</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Phallu is a son of Reuben.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d4">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1790121392</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
