<edge source="God" target="Sarah">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">God changed Sarai's name to Sarah, promised to bless Sarah, and promised that Sarah would bear Isaac and become a mother of nations.&lt;SEP&gt;God tells Sarah through Abraham that Sarah will bear a son and directly addresses Sarah's laughter about the promise.&lt;SEP&gt;Sarah laughs at the prospect of bearing a child in old age and later denies having laughed because she is afraid.&lt;SEP&gt;God visits Sarah and enables Sarah to conceive and bear a son.</data>
  <data key="d9">blessing,communication,fertility,laughter,promise,renaming,response</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121399</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="God" target="Abraham">
  <data key="d7">12.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Abraham and God is portrayed as one of divine revelation, covenant, guidance, and obedience. God appeared and spoke with Abraham, changed his name from Abram to Abraham, and established an everlasting covenant with him. God communicated with him about the birth and future of Isaac, Ishmael, Sarah, and Abraham’s household, instructing Abraham to heed Sarah and declaring that Abraham’s seed would be called through Isaac. God also caused Abraham to leave his father’s house and wander under divine direction.

Abraham responded by obeying God’s commands: he went to the place God designated, followed the command to travel to Moriah, and called on God’s name at Beersheba. He is identified as a prophet who prayed to God on behalf of Abimelech’s household. God remembered Abraham while destroying the cities and rescuing Lot, and is repeatedly identified as the God of Abraham. The relationship also includes promises concerning land: God gave land to Abraham, later associated with the inheritance promised to Jacob and his descendants, and swore an oath concerning the future land of the children of Israel. Abraham is further described as one of Jacob’s fathers who walked before God.</data>
  <data key="d9">ancestry,appearance,association,command,communication,covenant,hears command,instruction,land promise,oath,obedience,prayer,promise,promised land,prophecy,remembrance,renaming,worship,worships</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121405</data>
