<edge source="God" target="Jacob">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between God and Jacob is characterized by covenant, protection, guidance, blessing, and continuing presence. Jacob vowed that God would be his God and promised to give God a tenth of all the possessions he received. Jacob later attributed his children and prosperity to God’s gracious dealings, recalling that God answered him in distress, accompanied him throughout his journey, and blessed him.

God remained with Jacob during his years with Laban, saw Jacob’s affliction and labor, protected him from Laban’s attempts to harm him, and rebuked Laban. God commanded Jacob to leave that land and return to his ancestral kindred. God also appeared to Jacob at Bethel and again after his departure from Padanaram, affirming divine care and blessing.

In a nighttime vision, God instructed Jacob not to fear going to Egypt. Jacob described God as the one who had fed and shepherded him throughout his life, and expressed confidence that God would remain with Jacob’s descendants and eventually bring them back to their fathers’ land. God was also understood to have sworn an oath to Jacob concerning the future land of the children of Israel.</data>
  <data key="d9">answered,appeared,assistance,blessed,blessing,divine presence,grace,guidance,judgment,oath,promised land,protection,provision,revelation,vow,worship</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
