  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Abram" target="Lot">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lot traveled with Abram from Haran toward Canaan.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram and Lot separate after conflict between their herdsmen and divide their directions of travel.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram and Lot travel together from Egypt with their households and possessions.&lt;SEP&gt;Lot was Abram's brother's son, and Abram rescued Lot after Lot was captured.</data>
  <data key="d9">kinship,land division,rescue,separation,travel</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121399</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Abram" target="Canaan">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Abram traveled with Sarai and Lot into the land of Canaan.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram dwells in the land of Canaan after separating from Lot.</data>
  <data key="d9">destination,dwelling,settlement,travel</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121399</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Abram" target="LORD">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The LORD commanded Abram to leave his country and promised to bless Abram and make Abram a great nation.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram built altars to the LORD and called upon the name of the LORD.&lt;SEP&gt;The LORD appears to Abram, speaks to him, and is worshiped by Abram.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram invoked the LORD, identified as the Most High God and possessor of heaven and earth, when refusing to take Sodom's goods.&lt;SEP&gt;The word of the LORD comes to Abram in a vision, declaring protection and reward.&lt;SEP&gt;Abram believes in the LORD.</data>
  <data key="d9">altar,appearance,belief,blessing,command,devotion,faith,oath,reassurance,revelation,speech,worship</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121399</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
