<edge source="LORD" target="Abraham">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Abraham stands before the LORD and later observes the smoke rising from the destroyed cities.&lt;SEP&gt;The LORD fulfills and confirms the promise spoken concerning Abraham's son.&lt;SEP&gt;The LORD promised to bless Abraham, multiply his seed, and make his seed a blessing to all nations because Abraham obeyed.&lt;SEP&gt;The LORD blesses Abraham, and Abraham invokes the LORD as God of heaven and earth.&lt;SEP&gt;The LORD promised to perform the oath made to Abraham and to give countries to Abraham's seed.&lt;SEP&gt;Abraham obeyed the LORD's voice, charge, commandments, statutes, and laws.&lt;SEP&gt;The LORD identified himself to Isaac as the God of Abraham.</data>
  <data key="d9">blessing,commandments,communication,covenant,covenant promise,divine relationship,obedience,observation,promise,worship</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121408</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
