<edge source="Pharaoh" target="Joseph">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Joseph and Pharaoh encompasses Joseph’s rise from imprisonment to supreme authority in Egypt. Pharaoh summoned Joseph from the dungeon after learning of his ability to interpret dreams; one account specifies that the text does not explicitly state whether Joseph had already interpreted Pharaoh’s dream at the moment of the summons. Pharaoh subsequently appointed Joseph to govern all Egypt, making him “a father” to Pharaoh and lord over Pharaoh’s household and the land.

Joseph later presented his father, Jacob, and his brothers to Pharaoh and reported their arrival. During the famine, Joseph administered Egypt’s economy, collecting the people’s money and acquiring their land on Pharaoh’s behalf. When Jacob requested burial in Canaan, Joseph addressed the house of Pharaoh and formally asked Pharaoh for permission to bury his father. Pharaoh granted that request.</data>
  <data key="d9">administration,appointment,appoints,authority,burial arrangements,burial journey,communication,hears reputation,permission,presentation,service,summoned,summons</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121445</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
