<edge source="Sarah" target="Abraham">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sarah is identified as Abraham's wife.&lt;SEP&gt;Abraham and Sarah are married, and Sarah is also Abraham's paternal half-sister.&lt;SEP&gt;Sarah tells Abraham to cast out Hagar and Hagar's son.&lt;SEP&gt;Abraham came to mourn and weep for Sarah after her death.&lt;SEP&gt;Abraham is Sarah's husband and buries Sarah in the cave of Machpelah.</data>
  <data key="d9">burial,kinship,marriage,mourning,requests expulsion</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121405</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Isaac" target="Abraham">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Abraham, Isaac) describes Isaac as Abraham’s promised son and Abraham’s son. Abraham gives Isaac his name and, as his father, grants him all that he possesses.

Abraham takes Isaac to the land of Moriah, the designated offering place. There, Abraham binds Isaac and prepares to sacrifice him, presenting a central episode in their relationship. Abraham also seeks a wife for Isaac, acting to secure Isaac’s future and lineage.</data>
  <data key="d9">ancestry,family,father,fatherhood,inheritance,lineage,marriage arrangement,naming,parent,parentage,sacrifice,travel,travels with</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121408</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Isaac" target="Rebekah">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Rebekah is designated and accepted as Isaac's wife.&lt;SEP&gt;Rebekah is identified as Isaac's wife.&lt;SEP&gt;Isaac took Rebekah as his wife, loved Rebekah, and was comforted by the marriage.&lt;SEP&gt;Rebekah was Isaac's wife and heard Isaac instruct Esau to prepare food for a blessing.&lt;SEP&gt;Isaac and Rebekah were married.&lt;SEP&gt;Isaac and Rebekah are spouses and the parents of Jacob and Esau.</data>
  <data key="d9">family,love,marriage,parenthood</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027</data>
