<edge source="Isaac" target="Esau">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Isaac gives Esau a separate pronouncement concerning earthly dwelling, the sword, service to Jacob, and eventual release from Jacob's yoke.&lt;SEP&gt;Esau brings savory meat to Isaac and repeatedly asks Isaac for a blessing.&lt;SEP&gt;Isaac is Esau's father and loved Esau because Esau provided venison.&lt;SEP&gt;Esau is identified among the boys born to Isaac and Rebekah.&lt;SEP&gt;Isaac called Esau his eldest son and intended to bless him before his death.&lt;SEP&gt;Isaac is Esau's father, and Esau observes Isaac's blessing and sending away of Jacob.&lt;SEP&gt;Esau was Isaac's son and helped bury Isaac.</data>
  <data key="d9">affection,blessing,burial,family,fatherhood,parent,parent-child,parentage,requested blessing,secondary blessing,sonship</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121408</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Isaac" target="Jacob">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Isaac and Jacob is that Isaac was Jacob’s father, with Jacob identified as one of the boys born to Isaac and Rebekah. Jacob later presented himself to Isaac as Esau and, through this deception, received Isaac’s blessing.

Isaac also instructed Jacob not to marry a daughter of Canaan and sent him to Padanaram. Despite this departure, Jacob intended to travel to his father Isaac in the land of Canaan. Jacob referred to the God of his father Isaac in prayer, and he ultimately helped bury Isaac.</data>
  <data key="d9">blessing,burial,deception,family,father,fatherhood,instruction,parent,parent-child,parentage,prayer,sonship,travel</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121411</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
