<edge source="Laban" target="Jacob">
  <data key="d7">14.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Jacob and Laban began when Jacob fled to Laban after Rebekah warned him about Esau. Laban, Jacob’s maternal uncle, welcomed him into his household and hosted him for a month. Jacob then served Laban for agreed wages, particularly working as a shepherd and managing Laban’s livestock.

Jacob initially agreed to serve Laban for seven years in exchange for Rachel, and he subsequently agreed to serve additional years. In total, Jacob served Laban for twenty years: fourteen years for Laban’s two daughters and six years for Laban’s cattle. During this period, Laban repeatedly altered Jacob’s wages—described as happening ten times—and at one point placed a three-days’ journey between himself and Jacob while Jacob continued caring for the remainder of Laban’s flocks. Despite Laban’s efforts, God prevented him from harming Jacob.

Eventually, Jacob negotiated permission to leave with his family and possessions and departed while Laban was away. Jacob remained with Laban before sending messengers to Esau. Laban pursued Jacob, confronting him over the departure, the removal of his household possessions, and accusations arising from the search of Jacob’s camp. Jacob angrily challenged Laban over these accusations and over the hardships he had endured. The dispute ended when Laban proposed and established a covenant with Jacob as a witness between them.</data>
  <data key="d9">accusation,agreement,association,compensation,conflict,covenant,deception,dispute,distance,employment,family,host and guest,negotiation,nephew and uncle,refuge,residence,separation,service,travel,wage changes,wages</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-033</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121421</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
