<edge source="Esau" target="Jacob">
  <data key="d7">14.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Esau and Jacob are twin brothers, the sons of Isaac and Rebekah, with Esau born first. Their relationship includes a significant exchange in which Esau sold his birthright to Jacob after Jacob demanded it, and Esau swore to the agreement. Jacob then gave Esau bread and lentil pottage. Esau later identified Jacob as the brother who had taken both his birthright and Isaac’s blessing.

Because of Isaac’s blessing to Jacob, Esau hated Jacob and planned to kill him. Jacob consequently feared that Esau would attack him and his household. Later, Jacob sent messengers to Esau, who came to meet him. The brothers reconciled by embracing, kissing, and weeping together. Esau offered to leave some of the people accompanying him with Jacob, but ultimately moved away with his wives, children, household, cattle, and possessions. Their separation was attributed to the abundance of their riches and livestock, which made it impossible for them to dwell together.</data>
  <data key="d9">assistance,birthright,brotherhood,conflict,family,food,hostility,kinship,messengers,offer,provision,reunion,sale,separation,sibling relationship,siblings,siblingship,threat,twins</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-037</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121415</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
