<edge source="Joseph's Brothers" target="Joseph">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Joseph's brothers conspired to kill Joseph after seeing Joseph from a distance.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph questions his brothers, treats them as suspected spies, tests their claims, and supplies them with corn, money, and provisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph dines with his brothers, arranges a test involving the silver cup, and declares that the person possessing the cup will become a servant.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph forgave his brothers, promised to nourish them and their children, and comforted them.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph's brothers feared Joseph's retaliation and asked Joseph to forgive their wrongdoing.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph's brothers accompanied Joseph during the journey to bury Joseph's father.&lt;SEP&gt;Joseph's brothers had previously intended evil against Joseph.</data>
  <data key="d9">accusation,attempted killing,burial journey,conspiracy,family,fear,forgiveness,hospitality,interrogation,protection,provision,servitude,wrongdoing</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-054</data>
