<edge source="Rachel" target="Jacob">
  <data key="d7">12.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Jacob and Rachel is that of husband and wife. Jacob met Rachel at a well, where he watered the flock belonging to her father, Laban; he then kissed Rachel and wept. Jacob loved Rachel and agreed to serve Laban for seven years in order to marry her. After completing his service, he married Rachel, although the broader account also includes his marriage to Leah.

Rachel remained part of Jacob’s household during his departure from Laban. Jacob called Rachel to discuss leaving Laban, and Rachel responded in a conversation concerning the treatment and inheritance they had received from Laban’s household. Rachel traveled with Jacob when he left, and Jacob placed her and her household in the family procession as they approached Esau.

Rachel and Jacob were the parents of Joseph and Benjamin. Rachel later died near Jacob in the land of Canaan, and Jacob set up a pillar at her grave.</data>
  <data key="d9">affection,burial,communication,death,encounter,family,household arrangement,love,marriage,marriage proposal,parentage</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121427</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
