<edge source="Jacob" target="Leah">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Jacob and Leah were husband and wife in the biblical account. After Laban brought Leah to Jacob, Jacob went in unto her and she became his wife, although Jacob loved Rachel more and Leah was described as hated or less loved. Leah later arranged to spend the night with Jacob in exchange for her son’s mandrakes.

Leah and Jacob had several sons, including Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah. Leah was part of Jacob’s household when he decided to leave Laban; Jacob called her to discuss the departure, and Leah responded regarding the treatment she and her family had received and the inheritance withheld by Laban’s household. When Jacob traveled toward Esau, he placed Leah and her children within the family procession approaching Esau.</data>
  <data key="d9">affection,arrangement,communication,family,household arrangement,intimacy,marital preference,marriage,parentage,union</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121432</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Jacob" target="Judah">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Jacob was Judah's father.&lt;SEP&gt;Judah is Jacob's son.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacob sent Judah ahead of the family toward Goshen.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacob identifies Judah as his son and prophesies praise and victory for Judah.&lt;SEP&gt;Jacob blesses Judah and describes Judah’s future prominence, strength, and authority.</data>
  <data key="d9">blessing,delegation,family,father,parentage,prophecy</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121432</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Jacob" target="Joseph">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Jacob and Joseph is that of father and son. Joseph is identified as one of Jacob’s children and among the generations descending from Jacob. He accompanied Jacob and the rest of the family when Jacob met Esau. Jacob later mourned Joseph deeply after being led to believe that he had been devoured.

After Joseph entered Egypt and rose to authority, he nourished Jacob during the famine. Jacob eventually came to Egypt and reunited with Joseph in Goshen. During this period, Jacob identified Joseph as his son, requested that Joseph treat him kindly, and made him swear to bury Jacob outside Egypt rather than in Egypt. Joseph received this oath and later honored the request.

Before his death, Jacob bestowed abundant blessings upon Joseph, placing them on Joseph’s head. After Jacob died, Joseph fell upon his father’s face, wept over him, and kissed him, expressing his grief and filial devotion.</data>
  <data key="d9">affection,blessing,family,father,mourning,nourishment,oath,parentage,reunion,sonship</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053</data>
  <data key="d11">Book 01        Genesis.md</data>
  <data key="d12">1790121438</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Jacob" target="Israel">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Jacob receives the name Israel after prevailing in the struggle.&lt;SEP&gt;Israel is the name used for Jacob in the account of Jacob's arrival in Egypt.&lt;SEP&gt;The passage identifies Jacob with Israel and describes the twelve tribes of Israel as the sons whom Jacob blesses.&lt;SEP&gt;The passage uses Israel as the name of Jacob, including when Israel speaks to Joseph and Joseph's sons.</data>
  <data key="d9">alias,identity,name,name change,tribes</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a32a41554714252668fa190ace9e2f6c-chunk-053</data>
